-- title:
--   Stone flow: the distance to the exact states is conserved
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a self-adjoint generator with Stone flow $\mathrm{stoneU}$, and suppose the flow commutes with the gauge projection $\mathrm{Om}$.  Then for every $t$ and every $x$,
--   $$\mathrm{infDist}\big(\mathrm{stoneU}_t x, \mathrm{exactStates}\big) = \mathrm{infDist}\big(x, \mathrm{exactStates}\big).$$
--
--   This is the Stone-theorem form of the conservation statement: the abstract one-parameter flow of the previous theorem is here the flow generated by a self-adjoint operator, so the conservation of the BRST distance follows from spectral theory rather than from a group law assumed by hand.
--
--   Corrected statement of the retired node `BookProof.BrstReducedTransfer.infDist_exactStates_stoneU_eq`, whose target had lost the commutation hypothesis; it is explicit here.
-- source:
